#### How do I sign up for severe weather alerts and updates?

#### 1. Sign up for alerts and warnings about severe weather from your local emergency office.
**[Find local emergency alerts near you.](https://www.google.com/search?q=local+emergency+alerts+near+me&oq=local+emergency+alerts+near+me&)**
- Follow local authorities on social media for more informational updates. 

#### 2. Tune In
- Listen to the weather forecast on the radio, TV or weather app. 
- Listen to [NOAA's ALL HAZARDS WEATHER RADIO](https://www.weather.gov/nwr/): 
 - Broadcasts are found in the VHF public service band at these seven frequencies (MHz):
 162.400;
162.425;
162.450;
162.475;
162.500;
162.525;
162.550
- Monitor local weather reports
- Make sure your devices are charged, battery operated, or solar charging in case of power outage.

Additional Severe Weather Alert Options
- Download the [FEMA mobile App](https://www.fema.gov/about/news-multimedia/mobile-products#download) for additional alerts and updates on severe weather in the USA.
